= Web browser — Technical =

Modern browsers combine networking, parsing, rendering, scripting, storage, sandboxing, origin isolation, permissions, and accessibility subsystems. The final user-visible document can be the result of multiple resources and dynamic execution rather than one transferred file.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* web browser ≠ search engine
* browser ≠ Web itself
* rendered page ≠ source representation alone

== References ==
* W3C, ''Architecture of the World Wide Web, Volume One'', user-agent model.
